1
00:00:00,707 --> 00:00:02,417
(Sheldon:)Now, sit down.

2
00:00:02,960 --> 00:00:06,960
"I call your attention
to the events of November 16th.

3
00:00:07,130 --> 00:00:08,590
Do you remember that date?"

4
00:00:09,299 --> 00:00:12,089
"Darn tooting, I do.

5
00:00:13,595 --> 00:00:18,595
(Penny(reading):)If the court will excuse my homespun,
corn-fed, Nebraskan turn of phrase."

6
00:00:19,851 --> 00:00:23,141
(Sheldon:)-Excellent. Go on.
-"The reason that date is, like...

7
00:00:23,313 --> 00:00:27,443
(Penny:)...so totally fixed in my memory is that
I had the privilege to be witness...

8
00:00:27,609 --> 00:00:32,159
(Penny:)...to one of the most heroic acts
I've ever seen in, like, ever."

9
00:00:33,282 --> 00:00:36,322
"And who performed that heroic act?"

10
00:00:36,493 --> 00:00:40,333
"Why, you did, sir.
You, Dr. Sheldon Cooper.

11
00:00:40,497 --> 00:00:44,337
(Penny:)And may I add,
it is a privilege to know you."

12
00:00:44,835 --> 00:00:48,585
"There's no need for compliments.
This court is only interested in the facts."

13
00:00:48,755 --> 00:00:52,845
"But it is a fact
that it's a privilege to know you.

14
00:00:53,176 --> 00:00:55,136
Totally."

15
00:00:56,138 --> 00:00:59,018
"A teardrop rolls down my cheek"?

